[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-db.cxd — the database drivers' page,
   repo-cx-platform-db.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the db
   suite). A V product that ships no bundled module: its surface is seven
   builtins of the language, so the module table below is the generator's
   'no bundled module' note and the corpus is cited from conformance/. #]

[repo name=cx-platform-db
  [intro
    """**TL;DR — a database is a URL, and the rows come back as a document.**
       `cx-platform-db` is external database access: `$sql-open`,
       `$sql-exec`, `$sql-query` and `$sql-close`, `$redis-open`,
       `$redis-cmd` and `$redis-close` — builtins of the language, nothing
       to import — with the engine chosen by the URL's scheme: sqlite in the
       default build, redis, postgres and mysql as packs."""]
  [body
    """A query answers `[rows [row …]]`, a statement answers its change count
       and last row id, and every refusal is a value with a place in the
       order: an operand of the wrong kind is refused before any engine is
       consulted, an unknown handle is one uniform runtime error, closing a
       handle twice is `null` rather than a fault, and a constraint violation
       is an error carrying the backend's own state code — never an empty
       success. A refused multi-row statement leaves nothing behind."""]
  [body
    """Opening a connection is an effect, so it needs the `write` grant, and a
       connection URL that carries a credential is consumed at open — it
       never reaches a log line or an error message afterwards. Parameters
       bind by position as strings, and `[param null=true]` binds the
       backend's own NULL, which is what a keyset walk needs for the page
       before the first cursor. This is database access, not the CX store:
       `sqlite://` as a store substrate belongs to the [[store]] platform —
       two sqlites, one name."""]
  [gives
    """No module namespace: the surface is the seven builtins named above,
       specified in the repository's `db_access` page and graded by one
       corpus that covers every engine the default build carries. The
       registry names the repository through three rows — the suite and its
       two backends, `sql` and `redis` — none of them a module a program
       imports, so the table the generator draws for a module-shipping
       repository is the note below instead."""]
  [try
    """A whole lifecycle against an in-memory sqlite: open, create, insert,
       sum, close — the rows as a document, the grant on the command line
       because opening a database is an effect."""]
  [fixture id=db-010-sqlite-open-exec-query-close]
  [status
    """The drivers build on the language and are built on by the application
       host, their only in-tree consumer; the front door compiles the V
       module from the pin with the default engines, and a build without
       them answers that `sql-open` is not callable — a missing flag, not a
       defect."""]]
